<title>FINLAND: Rauma unit wins $65 mln fibre line order.</title>
<headline>Rauma unit wins $65 mln fibre line order.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Rauma Oy said in a statement on Tuesday that its Sunds Defibrator unit had won a $65 million order to supply a fibre line to German Kloeckner Industrie-Anlagen GmbH.</p>
<p>The pulping technology line would be supplied for the Musi pulp mill project in Indonesia to be jointly owned by PT Tanjung Enim Lestari Pulp &amp; Paper, Rauma said.  </p>
<p>Scheduled for start-up in 1999, the new pulp mill, designed to produce 450,000 tonnes per year of bleached market pulp, would be built in southern Sumatra.</p>
<p>&quot;The mill will be the first to exclusively use fast-growing acasia mangium as raw material for pulp production,&quot; Rauma said. --Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
